ty; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29c08583e0a27279baf7ded8e86fe2e42bf50b69.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29c08583e0a27279baf7ded8e86fe2e42bf50b69.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued July 28 at 5:00PM MDT until July 28 at 8:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nCentral Washington County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 830 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 500 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 1.5 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nAkron, Midway, Prewitt Reservoir, Lindon, Woodlin School,\nBurdett, Last Chance, Fremont Butte and Messex.","ends":"2026-07-28T20:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Morgan, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c0851e10bca4a627d6a374ccc189f2e8239d9408.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c0851e10bca4a627d6a374ccc189f2e8239d9408.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-07-28T23:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 282352 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 552 PM MDT Tue Jul 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to numerous storms expected TODAY and TOMORROW over the region; Storms capable of heavy rain - A few severe storms today, Flash flooding possible. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... Issued at 134 PM MDT Tue Ju